`-deps` no longer runs full semantic analysis on all imported modules

`-deps` used to force semantic analysis of every function body in every
imported module, just to find more dependencies. That made `-deps`
behave partly like `-i` without actually compiling those modules. It
slowed things down, listed dependencies that don't matter for
incremental builds, and could cause errors from library code that wasn't
being compiled, like `-betterC` errors from druntime.

Now `-deps` only reports what normal compilation finds. Imports inside
function bodies of modules that aren't being compiled are no longer
followed. To get the full transitive list, use `-deps` together with `-i`.
